{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/791648-dev-blog-on-gift-design-part-1","id":791648,"title":"[Dev Blog] On Gift Design Part 1","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-23T09:56:54-08:00","id":791648,"title":"[Dev Blog] On Gift Design Part 1","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-1-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\"> Santa Paws has come early folks!</a><br /> <br /> So, thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T11:56:55-08:00","id":791725,"title":"","content":"I like the Do's and Dont's spelled out, it will make designing Facets easier. I'm anxiously waiting for the second part. The new Cahalit Moon Gift is very cool but what I really want to see is more Wolf Gifts, those were by far my favourites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T13:46:46-08:00","id":791774,"title":"","content":"There's a new Shadow Gift and Wolf Gift coming in part 2 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T15:00:26-08:00","id":791806,"title":"","content":"I know! Hence the anxiousness <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also, Kudos on the new design behind Gifts and Facets, one of the best things from second edition in my humble opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T16:18:34-08:00","id":791841,"title":"","content":"I like the explanaition about the design, it's pretty exhaustive and pleasantly extensive. I dig how new gift works out and what was an intent, from fluff point of view it really works, reading it alone gives/adds to a PC concept. What I particularly love about the &quot;Do's&quot; is that Chris doesn't shy from going deep into &quot;you are a monstrous horror, everything about you should be as werewolf-y as possible&quot; territory to a point where he says outright to give to players means to &quot;terrorize a whole village&quot; (even though if this village nowadays is NYC). Thanks to it I realized that it's one of those things that I really like in 2ed - finally PC can be a werewolf that goes into the city after an unpenetrable, sudden mist engulfs all streets, where lights and telephones die when he passes, wind opens doors to his prey hideout and nature itself leads a prey into his mouth. Landscape and scene-changing stuff is very flavourful, in classic werewolf stories we have a mob of people rising to or being terrorized by a beast and here in mechanics we have something that can start narrative plothook. Very, very big plus for that entry and I'm waiting for the next one, especially for the wolf gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7871-miriander","name":"Miriander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T16:29:22-08:00","id":791844,"title":"","content":"It's exactly the type of thing I was looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T18:38:28-08:00","id":791896,"title":"","content":"It makes me wonder how these Gifts are bought, to be honest. I like that they're designed, but, lets say we use this in game. I don't imagine we'll learn them both the original and the new at once. Do we pick level by level? Choose one list at char gen and buy the other with EXP? Do we just spend Facet cost, or have to buy it as an entire new Gift?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T19:44:41-08:00","id":791921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/791648-dev-blog-on-gift-design-part-1?p=791896#post791896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes me wonder how these Gifts are bought, to be honest. I like that they're designed, but, lets say we use this in game. I don't imagine we'll learn them both the original and the new at once. Do we pick level by level? Choose one list at char gen and buy the other with EXP? Do we just spend Facet cost, or have to buy it as an entire new Gift?</div> </div> </div> </div>When you get your auspice renown, you learn a Moon Gift of equal rank, so you'll always have at least one Moon Gift at a dot rating equal to your auspice renown. A Cahalith who gets Glory 4 can't decide to get Screaming Moon 1, instead of Gibbous Moon 4, and because they don't have Screaming Moon 1-3, they can't get Screaming Moon 4.<br /> <br /> The matter of experience is covered in the Gaining Gifts and Facets section, p114. After talking about gaining facets of Moon Gifts from gaining renown, it points out, 'A werewolf may discover other Moon Gifts that are associated with her auspice at a cost of 5 Experiences, which unlocks the first dot Facet of the Gift. Gaining further Facets costs 2 Experiences each, and they must be purchased in ascending order. An Uratha can never raise the dots in a Moon Gift above the rating of her current auspice Renown.<br /> <br /> If you did manage to have both your auspice gifts up to the same level, with Screaming and Gibbous Moon at 4, when you get to 5 Glory, I imagine you can just pick which one you want for free. It would make sense and hardly be a game-breaker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-23-2015, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T23:20:34-08:00","id":792010,"title":"","content":"I feel the need to mention <i>that final facet.</i> It's wonderfully horrible. That's really <i>quite a lot of people</i> whose souls you'll be knocking off, if you do it anywhere heavily-populated...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T03:03:45-08:00","id":792072,"title":"","content":"I feel you should be able to harness those souls, to begin with. Yummy, yummy souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T05:03:24-08:00","id":792103,"title":"","content":"Here is a confession.<br /> I don't play Werewolf. I don't intend on playing it. I'm also not storytelling it, either. I didn't even really bother to read it in great detail, because while I appreciate it's quality as a game and how nicely written it is, and it's great themes, I don't like aesthetics of werewolf genre. However, I've read this blog post.<br /> Even without being a Werewolf player, it was really nice read. <br /> While I don't care about WWolf, I'm really interested in the design side of games. I feel that intelligent, structured approach to design with properly recognized and set goals is very important for game to be more than accidental success.<br /> This blog post is a design porn for me.<br /> <br /> It's presented in a neat, constructed and ordered way, it presents different elements with great precision, and provides context for the process of thoughts that it's showcasing. Even without being a Werewolf player, I can get a understanding of how the Gift blueprints work, and can appreciate how it was crafted. So...kudos <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T06:29:51-08:00","id":792135,"title":"","content":"Part 2 is up!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-2-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-2-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\"> The Giver of Gifts: 2 [Werewolf: The Forsaken] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-2-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-2-werewolf-the-forsaken/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T13:07:55-08:00","id":792326,"title":"","content":"I love the honor facts of the gift of cities. It's simply.... horrifying. Also, I love the suggestions of potential blasphemous wolf gifts. The gift of man, and gifts. Based on connections to other dark powers sounds really cool!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T13:19:00-08:00","id":792333,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Gift of Man made me think of Gaspode from Men At Arms. Hoping we can see that one some day.<br /> <br /> This is really cool. Maybe I'm just overlooking it but it always seemed to me that the rpg industry really neglects the storyteller side of things, when it comes to running games and stories and campaigns. And the actual works of game design have always seemed more scarce. Which makes sense because it looks like a personal thing but it's exceedingly helpful to see things like this.<br /> <br /> Thank you, so much.<br /> <br /> Also these gifts are just great. My dude's an elodoth but I've been clinging hard to the Technology facets, and the City ones are almost all 'things I've wanted to do but didn't have the ability to.' And Marrow Eater is my next get. Permanence and eating people? How could I say no?<br /> <br /> Essence Sight totally negates my side of an argument regarding power fuel gauges but I don't mind because it nicely rounds out the set. We'll probably just use loose narrative estimations than numbers, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-24-2015, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T05:17:58-08:00","id":792710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/791648-dev-blog-on-gift-design-part-1?p=791896#post791896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes me wonder how these Gifts are bought, to be honest. I like that they're designed, but, lets say we use this in game. I don't imagine we'll learn them both the original and the new at once. Do we pick level by level? Choose one list at char gen and buy the other with EXP? Do we just spend Facet cost, or have to buy it as an entire new Gift?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nofather's reply has the right of it. It's detailed in the Gifts section of the core book - we included the rules for buying additional Moon Gifts to future proof it even though I didn't have the space to actually feature extra Moon Gifts yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/791648-dev-blog-on-gift-design-part-1?p=792072#post792072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel you should be able to harness those souls, to begin with. Yummy, yummy souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I'm tempted to push towards Uratha-stolen souls working on the same framework from other sources too so that you can then hang merits off it, combo it with Lodges or whatnot.<br /> <br /> So, rites next then? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T05:32:58-08:00","id":792712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/791648-dev-blog-on-gift-design-part-1?p=792710#post792710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. I'm tempted to push towards Uratha-stolen souls working on the same framework from other sources too so that you can then hang merits off it, combo it with Lodges or whatnot.<br /> <br /> So, rites next then? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Reading between the lines that sounds a lot like the soul-stealing in Mage may be based on a framework that would generalise to other things. That could be fun...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T07:53:01-08:00","id":792742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/791648-dev-blog-on-gift-design-part-1?p=792710#post792710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, rites next then? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be great. The fine details of gifts always eluded me but the grand concept of 'spirit of the hunt' through the resonance of other concepts was easy. Rituals are tricker, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T14:38:54-08:00","id":792835,"title":"","content":"On the framework that rarer Wolf Gifts might require specific ways or methods to qualify for, I feel that the Gift Of Essence would be suited for the Lodge of the Field of Lycaon-Ur. It strikes me as a not unusual feature among their ilk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T15:55:41-08:00","id":792858,"title":"","content":"Isn't it ironic that the trappings of Wolf Gifts make them more suitable to be the discovery of individual lodges given their unlocking takes an arcane focus on their themes, when those are the most universal of gifts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 12-25-2015, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0