:[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T19:31:48-08:00","id":792912,"title":"","content":"Part two was sweet and even delicious! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> The City Gift was awesome and very handy for urban werewolves. I would defitnetly use this gift for my Iron Master character. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Though I would like to see the Gift of Man. Sounds frickin awesome!<br /> <br /> Wolf Gifts are my personal favorite gifts. I really like the Essence Gift. It will come in really handy. <br /> I really hope these awesome gifts become official in W:tF future books. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T09:09:10-08:00","id":793124,"title":"","content":"What I like about the take on Wolf Gifts is that with it one can have wolf-blooded families who passed knowledge of how to unlock a specific wolf gift through generations. I'm tempted to go with a grand-grand--grand-grandfather of PC who recently died passing him his diary dating back to 1800 or so and detailing his new life as Uratha and seeking a reason behind his condition that took him away from God, culminating with finding a new gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7871-miriander","name":"Miriander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}